[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :actor/wave 3, :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-dive-authorization-decision :finalize-dive-execution-decision :authorize-dive-to-proceed-directly :perform-dive-directly :execute-dive-directly :complete-dive-directly :override-dive-supervisor-judgment :override-dive-safety-officer-judgment :bypass-dive-supervisor :bypass-decompression-stop], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2799007232-cloud-itonami-isco-7232-aircraft-engine-mechanics-repairers-coverage"], :adr/status "accepted", :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["authorize the dive to proceed" "authorize the dive operation to proceed" "authorize the diver to descend" "clear the diver to descend" "clear the dive to proceed" "clear the dive operation to proceed" "finalize the dive authorization" "finalize the dive-authorization decision" "finalize the dive authorization decision" "finalize the dive execution decision" "finalize the dive-execution decision" "complete the dive directly" "perform the dive directly" "execute the dive directly" "execute the dive operation directly" "dispatch the diver to descend" "sign off the dive authorization" "sign the dive authorization" "issue the dive authorization" "override the dive supervisor's judgment" "override the dive supervisor" "override the dive safety officer's judgment" "override the diving safety officer's judgment" "override the dive-safety officer's judgment" "bypass the dive supervisor" "bypass the dive safety review" "bypass the decompression stop" "skip the decompression stop" "skip the required decompression stops"], :adr/id 2799007541, :actor/domain :maritime/underwater-dive-operation-scheduling-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:no-dive-operation :no-actuation :unknown-op :dive-operation-mismatch :unknown-diver :diver-wrong-dive-operation :scope-exclusion-violation], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7541", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007541: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7541 Underwater Divers dive-operation scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7541\n-- Underwater Divers** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of the rollout\n(Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3 batches 1-10 already landed: 60\noccupations so far).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7541\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7541\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Underwater Divers\" -- confirming\nthe premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity`\nwas `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics :identity\n:audit-ledger]`, `:optional-technologies []` and `:operating-states\n[:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit]`, and no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at `cloud-itonami/\ncloud-itonami-isco-7541` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before scaffolding).\nThis ADR and its companion registry edit promote the `7541` entry to\n`:implemented`.\n\n**This actor carries a life-safety-critical hazard framing comparable\nto the highest-stakes Wave3 batches so far (aviation-mechanic stakes):\nunderwater divers perform work where errors -- decompression sickness,\ndrowning, equipment failure at depth -- can cause death or serious\ninjury, categorically higher-stakes than ordinary workshop trades.**\nUnlike most workshop hazards, a diving error at depth often cannot be\ncorrected in the moment: a missed decompression stop, an undetected\nequipment fault or a misjudged current can become unrecoverable before\nthe diver can safely surface. The closed op allowlist therefore must\nNEVER include any op that directly finalizes a dive-authorization\ndecision (approving a dive to proceed) or a dive-execution decision,\nnor override a dive supervisor's/dive-safety-officer's judgment --\nthese are always a hard, permanent, structural block (absent from the\nallowlist entirely, not merely gated), never auto-commit-eligible\nunder any confidence level. Any safety/anomaly flag on a dive\noperation (equipment condition, decompression-table concern,\nweather/current condition) ALWAYS escalates, no exceptions, ever.\n\n**This actor coordinates DIVE-OPERATION SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS ONLY --\nit never performs diving work itself and never makes a\ndive-authorization decision.** It is not an authority to decide when\nor how a dive happens; it is a coordination layer for work-record\nlogging, crew/dive-team scheduling, safety-concern surfacing and\ndive-equipment/gas-supply order coordination, all gated behind an\nindependent governor. It never finalizes a dive-authorization decision\nand never performs or completes a dive.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7232`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7232)\n(Aircraft Engine Mechanics and Repairers: `store`/`advisor`/\n`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set,\nsame wave and the closest comparable life-safety-critical hazard\npattern already established in this fleet), cloned and read in full\nthis session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7541` as an OSS\ndocumentation/coordination actor for underwater divers, following the\nSAME governed-actor architecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*`\nactor in this fleet: **Dive Operation Scheduling/Logistics\nCoordination Advisor ⊣ DiveCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned\nidentically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different library\ncoordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger. All source is portable `.cljc` (no JVM interop); tests\nare `clojure.test` `.clj`, matching the reference repo's own layout.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- dive-log/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/dive-team/task scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface an equipment-condition/\n  decompression-table/weather-current concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER\n  auto-commit-eligible, no confidence-level exception, ever\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- dive-equipment/gas-supply procurement\n  proposal, escalates above a registered cost threshold\n\nNo op in this allowlist finalizes a dive-authorization decision\n(approving a dive to proceed), finalizes a dive-execution decision, or\noverrides a dive supervisor's/dive-safety-officer's judgment -- these\ndecision classes are structurally absent from the allowlist, not\nmerely gated behind escalation.\n\n### Six HARD governor checks (`divecoord.governor`, permanent, never\noverridable by human approval)\n\n1. **no-dive-operation** -- the dive-operation/dive-team record must\n   be independently verified/registered before any action.\n2. **no-actuation** -- proposal `:effect` must be `:propose` (the\n   governor never dispatches hardware and never performs diving\n   work).\n3. **unknown-op** -- `:op` must be one of the four allowlisted\n   coordination ops; the closed op-allowlist is enforced\n   unconditionally.\n4. **dive-operation-mismatch** -- if the proposal names a\n   dive-operation, it must be the SAME dive-operation verified for\n   this request (defense-in-depth against a proposal quietly\n   targeting an unverified dive-operation).\n5. **unknown-diver / diver-wrong-dive-operation** -- if the proposal\n   references a diver, that diver must be a REGISTERED certified crew\n   member belonging to this dive-operation.\n6. **scope-exclusion-violation** -- a proposal that attempts, in any\n   free-text field, to authorize a dive to proceed, to finalize a\n   dive-execution decision, or to override a dive supervisor's or\n   dive-safety-officer's judgment is a HARD, PERMANENT block,\n   evaluated unconditionally on content, independent of `:op`.\n\n### Escalation gates, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (`divecoord.governor/always-escalate-ops`). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface an equipment-condition/\n  decompression-table/weather-current concern -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and this is unconditional: no confidence level,\n  however high, ever exempts a safety flag from human sign-off.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-order-cost-threshold` (20000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-or-below-cost-threshold`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence.\n- advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` (0.6) also escalates,\n  for any op.\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare nouns (e.g.\n\"dive\", \"depth\", \"decompression\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this risk is especially\nsharp here because this actor's ENTIRE domain is underwater diving\noperations, so bare nouns like \"dive\"/\"depth\"/\"decompression\"/\"gas\nmix\"/\"descent\" are ordinary, unavoidable vocabulary.\n`divecoord.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTION PHRASES (e.g. \"authorize the dive to\nproceed\", \"finalize the dive execution decision\", \"override the dive\nsupervisor's judgment\"), never bare nouns, and\n`divecoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor (including a\n`:flag-safety-concern` request whose description names a \"regulator\nfree-flow observed during pre-dive check, unresolved\ndecompression-table concern pending review\"), never trips the\nscope-exclusion guard. A companion test,\n`scope-exclusion-not-triggered-by-bare-domain-nouns`, asserts directly\nagainst `governor/scope-exclusion-violation?` that a rationale/\ndescription containing only bare domain nouns (\"dive team on wreck\ninspection at 30 meters depth with staged decompression\", \"diver fully\ncertified for saturation diving ... gas mix documentation for this\ndive\") does not trip the guard, while\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-authorize-dive-to-proceed`,\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-finalize-dive-execution-decision`,\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-finalize-dive-authorization`,\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-override-dive-supervisor`,\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-override-dive-safety-officer`\nand\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-bypass-decompression-stop`\nconfirm the actual forbidden action phrases DO trip it, and\n`holds-a-scope-excluded-proposal-with-no-interrupt-path`,\n`holds-a-finalize-dive-execution-proposal-with-no-interrupt-path` and\n`holds-an-override-dive-supervisor-proposal-with-no-interrupt-path`\nconfirm the full actor graph resolves such attempts straight to\n`:hold` (a finish point, never `:request-approval`) with no record\ncommitted.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7541\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7541` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7541`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit to account for concurrent sibling landings in this\n  same batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 28 tests, 72 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a fresh clone of the pushed repository (mojibake scan: 0\n  replacement characters found).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n- Full doc set published: README.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md,\n  CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE\n  (AGPL-3.0-or-later, byte-identical to the `cloud-itonami-isco-7232`\n  reference's LICENSE text), docs/business-model.md,\n  docs/operator-guide.md, blueprint.edn.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-dive-authorization` or\n  `:authorize-dive` that is merely gated behind `always-escalate-ops`:\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit diving-safety guidance --\n  an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  dive-authorization decision exists in the code path and is merely\n  deferred to a human gate. For a decision that can directly cost\n  lives underwater with limited opportunity for in-descent correction,\n  the capability itself must not exist in the allowlist at all --\n  this matches the strict bar already established by\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7232` for airworthiness-clearance/return-to-\n  service determinations.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"dive\" \"depth\"\n  \"decompression\"]`): rejected per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class -- this actor's entire domain is underwater diving operations,\n  so bare nouns would self-trip on essentially every legitimate\n  proposal (work-record logs naming \"inspect pier pile joint at 18\n  meters depth\", crew-schedule proposals naming \"dive team\", safety\n  flags naming \"decompression-table concern\", supply orders naming\n  \"twinset cylinders and surface-supply umbilical\", etc.).\n- Checking dive-operation/diver provenance only from the proposal\n  (never the request): rejected -- the dive-operation-mismatch check\n  requires the dive-operation identity to be anchored at the request\n  level and independently cross-checked against anything the proposal\n  claims, so a proposal that quietly names a different, unverified\n  dive-operation is caught even if the proposal otherwise looks\n  well-formed.\n- Modeling the diver-registration check as unconditionally required on\n  every op: rejected as too rigid -- `:coordinate-supply-order`\n  legitimately has no diver to reference (it is a materials-\n  procurement proposal against the dive-operation, not a person); the\n  check applies only when a proposal actually references a\n  `:diver-id`.\n- Folding the dive-authorization hazard into the same generic\n  \"execution\" phrase family used by the aircraft-engine reference (no\n  dive-authorization-specific phrases): rejected -- a dive-\n  authorization decision (approving a dive to proceed) is materially\n  distinct from a generic \"perform the dive directly\" phrase (a\n  proposal could name a dive-authorization sign-off specifically\n  without using generic execution language), so dedicated phrases\n  (\"authorize the dive to proceed\", \"clear the diver to descend\",\n  \"finalize the dive authorization\", \"sign off the dive\n  authorization\", \"issue the dive authorization\") and a dedicated\n  regression test\n  (`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-authorize-dive-to-proceed`)\n  were added independently of the generic dive-execution phrases. A\n  further dedicated phrase pair (\"bypass the decompression stop\",\n  \"skip the decompression stop\") and regression test\n  (`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-bypass-decompression-stop`)\n  cover the diving-specific hazard of a proposal attempting to\n  short-circuit a required decompression stop, which has no analogue\n  in the aircraft-engine reference.\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 20000}", :test/counts "{:total 28, :assertions 72, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Underwater Dive Operation Scheduling & Logistics Coordination Service", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :dive-operation-verification :diver-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-order-cost-threshold-escalation :always-escalate-safety-concern :dive-authorization-scope-exclusion :dive-execution-finalization-scope-exclusion :dive-supervisor-override-scope-exclusion :dive-safety-officer-override-scope-exclusion :decompression-stop-bypass-scope-exclusion], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7541", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7541", :adr/scope ["cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7541" "kotoba-lang/occupation"], :test/simulator :divecoord.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7541 — Underwater Divers Dive-Operation Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7541}]